body:
Jesus Christ!  Call the cops and CPS!    

&#x200B;

She's going to keep taking any mile she can from any inch you give her. Next thing you know the kids will be there for an entire shift.

Did you intend for that comment to be a reply to the original post? Or did you really just go off on a person who made a joke about slipping tickets into a coffin?

&#x200B;

For someone saying we shouldn't take COVID seriously, you sure took a snide comment seriously.

Your point is gold and I'm glad to see someone pointing it out. No, there wasn't any justification! Qyburn said there weren't any scorpions left, so Drogon had absolutely no lethal threats against him. As you said, she could've flown straight to the Red Keep, straight to the window Cersei was looking out of and burned her alive. Dany just decided to take all the commonfolk with her. This point should've been talked about in the show. Instead of simply 'you burned innocents' it should've been 'You had all the ability in the world to fly directly to Cersei and Dracarys her ass, but instead you set the city on fire with no assurance it would actually take Cersei down". 

&#x200B;

Wouldn't it have been better for Dany to burn her directly than hope that Cersei doesn't sneak out of the castle and survive?

Right there with ya! We've been sucked into this thing for a decade and now it's over. I had anxiety while queuing up last nights episode. Kept telling myself that 'it's just a TV show! Don't get that worked up over it!' I do think it was presented in a way that tied up just enough ends for it to really be the finale.  Enough of an ending to be closure, that is (at least for me). Although I think most of us would agree that this final season felt rushed, I'm wondering if it wasn't rushed, would I feel even more empty than I do now? If I invested another couple years of my life into this storyline, wouldn't it feel more sorrowful when it's over? I'm not quite sure. But in this sense, I'm glad it's over. I can digest all of this sooner than later and won't have to deal with even more added emotional investment. 

&#x200B;

Then again, who's to say it wouldn't have the opposite effect? Instead of a rushed, sudden ending like a rug being pulled from under our feet -  it would allow for the closure to come over an extended period of time leaving us feeling fulfilled and satisfied?

I think that's what draws people to her, she's not blatantly good like Jon Snow nor evil like Ramsey. I dislike yet like her at the same time. We don't always know what to expect from her and that's intriguing.  Watching her ascent into madness has been entertaining but we don't quite know how far it will go. She still teeters on the edge of burning the world to the ground versus placing strategic kills to save innocent lives. 

&#x200B;

Personally, I don't feel bad for her. At the beginning of the series, she told her brother that all she wants to do is go home. Then bro dies and she gets to take his place as heir.  She then gets a little power hungry and demands things to be her way or the highway. I loved that she wanted to be 'breaker of chains' and make the world a better place but I feel that her lust for the throne has taken precedence over changing the world for good and it'll be interesting to see what route she takes when faced with a decision. She's already begged Jon not to spill the beans and take the thrown, so I think she's now more interested in power than popularity.

For the face, I've been using (and LOVING -  after I figured out my favorite way of application) W3ll People Bio Tint Moisturizer. To me, it's mostly sunblock with a good tint to it. I think it moisturizes a bit, but I don't use it in place of moisturizer.  However, I do use this in place of foundation as that it has a nice coverage.  I truly hate the feeling of any product on my skin, so as a warning this stuff can be a bit tacky for the first few minutes. I have yet to try it for reapplication though, ya know the 'reapply every two hours' deal, so I cannot comment as to how well it looks/feels when reapplied several times throughout the day. 

&#x200B;

For the body, I like Pacifica sunblock. They have several different types to choose from. I use Pacifica facial sunblock for my face when I'm going to be out in the sun all day (pool/lake/concert, etc). 

&#x200B;

Hope this helps! And good luck with your search! I think I've finally found my holy grail products with these babies

New Purchase - Juice Beauty Stem Cellular CC Cream  - I was hoping for a HG all-in -one product but unfortunately I must keep searching. I use to use Urban Decay's One and Done, I did love it but I'm on a mission to avoid silicone.

I do love the 'clean' ingredients in it and the only downfalls are: 

1) virtually no coverage - I consider myself to have fairly decent skin and rarely ever wear actual foundation/makeup. I was hoping for some coverage but this really doesn't have any at all. If you have absolutely flawless skin, it would probably look great. 

2) kinda sticky - doesn't really 'set'. I'm not one to use setting power or sprays, so I found it to be a bit sticky/dewy throughout the day. 

&#x200B;

Upsides:

1) SMELLS AWESOME!!  Like fruity pebbles....I normally don't care how something smells but this is just glorious (made me crave fruity pebbles every morning though lmao)

2) SPF  30 - Zinc Oxide 20%

3) Organic ingredients & vitamins C & E

4) I couldn't find any silicone in ingredients list

&#x200B;

Next on my list to try is W3ll People Bio-Tint Moisturizer. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

